IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g7-commencement`
IMPORT `g8-fees`

-- ind-c-tests-commencement.l4: independent tests (ind-c) of s.63(b), the commencement of Chapter 6, which gates
-- every rule of my scope (gazette p. 198), and of the commencement day of s.63(a)(1) it counts from.
-- The publication day 14.1.2025 is printed at the foot of every gazette page; the s.59 regulations (the Fees
-- Regulations as made) came into force 7 days from their publication on 9.7.2025, so on 16.7.2025.
-- Scenario ids are those of work/ind-c/expectations.md.

§ `ind-c: s 63(b)`

§§ `Fixtures`

GIVEN s46 IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A `Facts that fix the commencement of the Law under section 63`
`ind-c the facts, the s 46 regulations being in force from` s46 MEANS
    `Facts that fix the commencement of the Law under section 63` WITH
        `the day the Law was published in Reshumot` IS YMD 2025 1 14
        `the s.59 regulations came into force on` IS `the Fees Regulations made under section 59 came into force on`
        `the day regulations under section 46 came into force, if any` IS s46

§§ `G1-G6`

-- The s.59 regulations: in force 2025-07-16 (reg 5: seven days from 2025-07-09).
#ASSERT `the Fees Regulations made under section 59 came into force on` EQUALS YMD 2025 7 16
-- G1: the commencement day: the later of 2025-04-14 (three months after 2025-01-14) and 2025-07-16.
#ASSERT `the commencement day under section 63(a)(1)` (`ind-c the facts, the s 46 regulations being in force from` NOTHING) EQUALS YMD 2025 7 16
-- G2/G3: s.46 regulations in force 2026-12-01: Chapter 6 commences 18 months after 2025-07-16, Saturday 2027-01-16.
#ASSERT `the day Chapter 6 commences under section 63(b)` (`ind-c the facts, the s 46 regulations being in force from` (JUST (YMD 2026 12 1))) EQUALS YMD 2027 1 16
-- G4: s.46 regulations in force 2027-03-01, later: Chapter 6 commences 2027-03-01.
#ASSERT `the day Chapter 6 commences under section 63(b)` (`ind-c the facts, the s 46 regulations being in force from` (JUST (YMD 2027 3 1))) EQUALS YMD 2027 3 1
-- G5: with G3's facts, an act on 2027-01-15 is before Chapter 6; an act on 2027-01-16 is not.
#ASSERT NOT (`Chapter 6 was in force on the day of the act` (YMD 2027 1 15) `given the facts` (`ind-c the facts, the s 46 regulations being in force from` (JUST (YMD 2026 12 1))))
#ASSERT `Chapter 6 was in force on the day of the act` (YMD 2027 1 16) `given the facts` (`ind-c the facts, the s 46 regulations being in force from` (JUST (YMD 2026 12 1)))
-- With G4's facts: 2027-02-28 before, 2027-03-01 in force.
#ASSERT NOT (`Chapter 6 was in force on the day of the act` (YMD 2027 2 28) `given the facts` (`ind-c the facts, the s 46 regulations being in force from` (JUST (YMD 2027 3 1))))
#ASSERT `Chapter 6 was in force on the day of the act` (YMD 2027 3 1) `given the facts` (`ind-c the facts, the s 46 regulations being in force from` (JUST (YMD 2027 3 1)))
-- G6, the rejected alternative (s.10(c) applied to a commencement, kind C), Saturday 2027-01-16 a rest day: 2027-01-17.
#ASSERT `s 63(b) — the day Chapter 6 commences, under the readings` (`ind-c the facts, the s 46 regulations being in force from` (JUST (YMD 2026 12 1))) (`the readings of the dates with IL s.10(c) applied, for the calendar` (`Calendar of rest days` WITH `days of rest, recess or holiday` IS LIST (YMD 2027 1 16))) EQUALS YMD 2027 1 17
-- X7 (ambiguity): no s.46 regulations are known.  The text gives no answer (one reading: Chapter 6 never
-- commences; the other: 18 months).  Asserted: the encoding does not invent a date.
#ASSERT REFUSED `the day Chapter 6 commences under section 63(b)` (`ind-c the facts, the s 46 regulations being in force from` NOTHING)
-- An act BEFORE the 18 months is not under Chapter 6 whatever s.46 says.
#ASSERT NOT (`Chapter 6 was in force on the day of the act` (YMD 2027 1 15) `given the facts` (`ind-c the facts, the s 46 regulations being in force from` NOTHING))
